n class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> recognises Euthydemus and offers a daughter to his son Demetrius</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">190–180 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Demetrius invades north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-greek-kingdom">Indo-Greek Kingdom</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 171 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Eucratides seizes power in a coup and founds the Eucratid dynasty</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 145 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Eucratides is killed by his own son; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ai-khanoum">Ai-Khanoum</a> is burnt during nomadic invasions</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 120 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> expand into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and Heliocles moves his capital to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> valley</span></li></ol>
